pe/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-282147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=-4i+3k$ and $b=i+2j-2k.$ Find $a\\times b.$\n\n$a\\times b=$\n\n{{field-1}}$\\,i\\,-\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,j\\,-\\,$\n{{field-3}}$\\,k$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-282147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0)(-2)-(3)(2)i-(-4)(-2)-(3)(1)j+(-4)(2)-(0)(1)k \\\\  & =(0-6)i-(8-3)j+(-8-0)k \\\\  & =-6\\,i-5\\,j-8\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-282147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2b0550090cc26f93266a7b0f166dd854d1a1cbe6f6ecc0508c6c1b68bfd5def3"} {"question" "q-282147" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-282147" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-282147" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-282147" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-282147" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-282147" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-103542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨-1,2x,3⟩,$ $b=⟨2,-x,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{355}.$ Find $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-103542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 2x & 3 \\\\ 2 & -x & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ -x & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2x \\\\ 2 & -x\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2x+3x)i-(-1-6)j+(x-4x)k \\\\  & =⟨5x,7,-3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(5x)^{2}+(7)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{x}^{2}+49+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34{x}^{2}+49}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{355} \\\\ \\sqrt{34{x}^{2}+49} & =\\sqrt{355} \\\\ 34{x}^{2}+49 & =355 \\\\ 34{x}^{2} & =306 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-103542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2b0550090cc26f93266a7b0f166dd854d1a1cbe6f6ecc0508c6c1b68bfd5def3"} {"question" "q-103542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-103542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-3,9"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{3},3"] ["math" "x=\\pm 3"] ["math" "x=\\pm 9"] ["math" "x=\\pm \\frac{1}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-103542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\pm 3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-77427" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨2,x,1⟩,$ $b=⟨1,-x,3⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=10.$ Find $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-77427" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & x & 1 \\\\ 1 & -x & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ -x & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & x \\\\ 1 & -x\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3x+x)i-(6-1)j+(-2x-x)k \\\\  & =⟨4x,-5,-3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+25+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25({x}^{2}+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =10 \\\\ \\sqrt{25({x}^{2}+1)} & =10 \\\\ 25({x}^{2}+1) & =100 \\\\ {x}^{2}+1 & =4 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-77427" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2b0550090cc26f93266a7b0f166dd854d1a1cbe6f6ecc0508c6c1b68bfd5def3"} {"question" "q-77427" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-77427" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=\\pm 2"] ["math" "x=\\pm 3"] ["math" "x=\\pm 4"] ["math" "x=\\pm \\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-77427" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-282270" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨x,1,2⟩,$ $b=⟨1,0,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{5}.$ Find $x.$\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-282270" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(2x-2)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =⟨2,2-2x,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(2-2x)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+(4{x}^{2}-8x+4)+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-8x+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-8x+9} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-8x+9 & =5 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-8x+4 & =0 \\\\ (2x-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-282270" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2b0550090cc26f93266a7b0f166dd854d1a1cbe6f6ecc0508c6c1b68bfd5def3"} {"question" "q-282270" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-282270" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-103540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨2x,3,2⟩$, $b=⟨x,1,-1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{93}.$ Find $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-103540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 3 & 2 \\\\ x & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 2 \\\\ x & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ x & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-3-2)i-(-2x-2x)j+(2x-3x)k \\\\  & =⟨-5,-4x,x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-4x)^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+16{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{93} \\\\ \\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+25} & =\\sqrt{93} \\\\ 17{x}^{2}+25 & =93 \\\\ 17{x}^{2} & =68 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-103540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2b0550090cc26f93266a7b0f166dd854d1a1cbe6f6ecc0508c6c1b68bfd5def3"} {"question" "q-103540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-103540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-2,4"] ["math" "x=-4,2"] ["math" "x=4"] ["math" "x=\\pm 2"] ["math" "x=\\pm 4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-103540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\pm 2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨2x,1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨3,0,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{157}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(4x-12)j+(0-3)k \\\\  & =⟨2,12-4x,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(12-4x)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+(144-96x+16{x}^{2})+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-96x+157}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{157} \\\\ \\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-96x+157} & =\\sqrt{157} \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-96x+157 & =157 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-96x & =0 \\\\ 16x(x-6) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,x=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=0,$ $x=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2b0550090cc26f93266a7b0f166dd854d1a1cbe6f6ecc0508c6c1b68bfd5def3"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "d10a27fa6c765bdbd17de87aa5782ab7f7ad7c81a6a74734775fb7382088e395"} {"question" "e-4341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3,-4,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -7,0,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/example-4341.json" "file_sha256" "5b668d7430ddd4c028760aa614195673a81303fedb7034b9cb195a85b17410e3"} {"question" "e-4341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -7 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 0)i-(3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-7))j+(3\\cdot 0-(-4)\\cdot (-7))k \\\\  & =-8i-13j-28k \\\\  & =⟨-8,-13,-28⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/example-4341.json" "file_sha256" "5b668d7430ddd4c028760aa614195673a81303fedb7034b9cb195a85b17410e3"} {"question" "e-4343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3, 1, 2x \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,1,x \\rangle,$ and $|\\,\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\,| = \\sqrt{19}.$ Find $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/example-4343.json" "file_sha256" "5b1ad67bf4163862d73eb7ca033ee82505799922d4112761bee1e65679443669"} {"question" "e-4343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2x \\\\ 0 & 1 & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2x \\\\ 1 & x\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2x \\\\ 0 & x\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-xi-3xj+3k \\\\  & =⟨-x,-3x,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-x)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & |\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & \\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}+9=19 \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}=10 \\\\  & {x}^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x= \\pm 1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/example-4343.json" "file_sha256" "5b1ad67bf4163862d73eb7ca033ee82505799922d4112761bee1e65679443669"}] "usage" {"e-4341" [] "q-103542" [] "q-103540" [] "e-4343" []} "basis" 1385 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186303441 17592186303442 17592186303443 17592186303444 17592186303445 17592186303448 17592186303449 17592186303450 17592186303451 17592186303452] "immutable_fields" [[17592186303440 :answer-field/correct] [17592186303440 :answer-field/id]